	'about_b1_p1' => 'Mara Lindqvist and Kwame Asante founded Zaseki Panel in 2022. Operating from Unit 4 at Ferrow Yard, 18 Canal Street in Norrbridge, our workshop focuses on building simple, reliable hardware for shared workplaces. Mara directs product design, creating matte wall panels that present clear architectural layouts without digital clutter. Kwame oversees the electronics, firmware, and low-power round desk tags. We assemble each panel by hand, calibrate display cells, and test radio communication before shipping crates to customer buildings.',
	'about_b2_p1' => 'Our five-person team manages every stage of production, planning, and installation. Mara Lindqvist serves as co-founder and leads product design, refining the physical enclosure and visual grid. Kwame Asante is co-founder leading electronics and desk tags, developing the radio protocol and battery power systems. Priya Raman directs building installations, managing on-site mounting and staff walk-throughs. Daniel Okafor conducts building surveys, measuring layouts and checking Wi-Fi and power. Élodie Marchand manages the pre-order desk, answering customer enquiries and scheduling build slots.',
	'about_b3_p1' => 'A typical working day demonstrates how the hardware functions across office hours. At 08:10, front-desk staff switch on lobby lights, where the panel already shows yesterday\'s tags released and all desks reset to sage. By 08:40, the first wave of morning arrivals taps the panel to hold desks. At 10:00, any held desks that were never claimed tap out automatically, returning to sage. During lunch at 13:00, occupied desks remain stone. At 17:30, members tap out, returning the floor to sage overnight.',
	'about_b4_p1' => 'We welcome visitors to see the panels in person and watch tag assembly at our Norrbridge facility. Workshop visits take place on Thursdays between 14:00 and 16:00, strictly by appointment. During your visit, you can test the wall panel, handle desk tags, examine mounting brackets, and discuss floor plans directly with Mara and Kwame. To schedule an appointment, contact Élodie at our pre-order desk at hello@zaseki-panel.example with your preferred Thursday date.',
