	'floor_p1' => 'In most shared offices the day starts with a lap. People walk the long aisles and look into every bay for an empty chair, and too often a desk that looks free from across the room turns out to hold a notebook, a jacket or a bag. The lap costs ten minutes, and everyone who joins the floor later does it again.',
	'floor_p2' => 'By nine, the front desk takes the strain. Receptionists are asked whether anywhere is free forty times before ten o\'clock, which interrupts the work they are there to do and builds a small queue in the foyer while newcomers wait to be pointed at a chair on another floor.',
