	'install_b1_p1' => 'Two to three weeks before installation day, Daniel surveys your building. He checks the wall construction, confirms socket locations within three metres of the planned mounting point, records the exact desk count, and tests local Wi-Fi coverage across the floor. From this survey visit, we draw your custom floor plan showing up to 120 desks. We review the draft plan with you prior to the install date so every desk position matches your physical layout.',
	'install_b2_p1' => 'Priya and her installation team complete each floor in a single day. The team mounts the wall bracket at a 140 centimetre centre height, secures the 55 by 38 centimetre panel, and connects the three metre power cable to your dedicated wall socket. Small round desk tags are fixed to the edge of every desk using adhesive pads, and the team pairs each tag with its corresponding position on the wall panel\'s display.',
	'install_b3_p1' => 'Once hardware is secured and tested, Priya leads a twenty minute walk-through with your front desk and facilities team. Staff learn how the panel operates, how visitors hold a desk from the lobby, how desk tags switch indicators from clay to stone, and how unclaimed holds reset to sage after fifteen minutes. After the walk-through is finished, the remaining balance is invoiced, payable in thirty days.',
	'install_b4_p1' => 'To prepare for installation day, your building provides four simple elements. First, a clear interior wall space suitable for mounting the bracket at 140 centimetre centre height. Second, one standard wall power socket located within three metres of the panel. Third, working Wi-Fi network access reaching the lobby and desk areas. Fourth, one nominated contact person who can grant building access and attend the twenty minute walk-through at the end of the day.',
	'install_b5_p1' => 'Following installation, buildings can maintain ongoing support through the Zaseki Care Plan at EUR 180 per panel per year. The care plan includes replacement spare parts, remote software updates, and direct phone help from our team. If you ever rearrange your furniture or add workstations, we provide floor-plan updates for EUR 90, redrawing your layout and updating your panel remotely without requiring an on-site visit.',
