	'no_posts' => 'No notes yet.',
	'panel_b1_p1' => 'When you walk into the lobby, tap any free desk on the wall panel. The chosen desk turns clay immediately and remains held for fifteen minutes while you make your way upstairs or across the floor. This brief reservation gives you time to hang your coat, carry your bag to the desk, and get settled without rushing or worrying that someone else might sit down before you arrive.',
	'panel_b2_p1' => 'At the desk, tap the small round desk tag fixed to the desk edge. The tag registers your arrival, and the indicator on the lobby panel turns from clay to stone, marking the desk as taken. It remains taken throughout your working day until you tap out when leaving. If you step away for lunch or a meeting, the desk stays taken so your workspace remains yours.',
	'panel_b3_p1' => 'If nobody taps the desk tag within fifteen minutes of the initial lobby tap, the hold lets go by itself. The desk returns to sage on the wall panel, showing everyone on the floor that the seat is free once again. This automatic release ensures that forgotten holds or changed plans never leave desks blocked for other members arriving later in the morning.',
	'panel_b4_p1' => 'Each Zaseki Panel measures 55 by 38 centimetres, sits 14 millimetres deep on the wall, and weighs 2.1 kilograms. Finished with a matte pale face, a single panel displays an abstract floor plan of up to 120 desks. Power comes from a single wall adapter plugged into a standard socket with a 3 metre cable. Every desk is fitted with a small round desk tag attached by an adhesive pad and powered by a replaceable coin cell. Desks show three clear states: sage indicates free, clay indicates held, and stone indicates taken.',
	'panel_b5_p1' => 'Each floor shipment arrives in one crate containing four main components. The wall panel is ready for mounting, accompanied by a wall bracket and a 3 metre power cable. Packs of round desk tags arrive with adhesive pads and fresh coin cells ready for each desk edge. Your building floor plan is drawn once from the survey and loaded into the panel. The crate also includes front-desk quick reference cards, spare desk tags, and a mounting template for installation.',
